  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2003-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(X = \\log x\\) and \\(Y = \\log y.\\) Then \\[X + 3Y = 1\\] and \\[2X + Y = 1.\\]\n\nSolving gives \\(X = \\dfrac{2}{5}\\) and \\(Y = \\dfrac{1}{5},\\) so \\[ \\log(xy) = X + Y = \\frac{3}{5}. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Let \\(X = \\log x\\) and \\(Y = \\log y;\\) the equations become linear in \\(X\\) and \\(Y\\)",
        "Solve \\(X + 3Y = 1\\) and \\(2X + Y = 1,\\) then compute \\(X + Y\\)"
      ],
